# `go` is called ahead of the store of `held`, with no turn. It does not read `held`: `read` does, whose body is copied into the loop. The type of that read leaves out "not yet filled" because no reader can start ahead
# of the store: true where the read stands, and carried by no operand. What stands in front of a loop runs though the loop has no turn. So in front of the typed copy the word is read as it lies and asked; what is
# empty goes to the closed copy, where the read stands in its turn; the unboxing and the load of the slot stand behind the test. f1 = go.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: absent|{{*}} = GetModuleVariable {{*}}givesWordAsItLies
# CHECK-NEXT: = TypeTest {{*}}testedType=absent
# CHECK: = Narrowed
# CHECK-NEXT: = Unbox
# CHECK-NEXT: = GetSlot {{*}}key="width"
